@startuml state-circuit-breaker
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "JetBrains Mono"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam BorderColor #444444

title CircuitBreaker State Machine — ResilienceLayer — Apollia OS

[*] --> Closed

state Closed #1a1a2e/e0e0ff : Tool calls pass through normally.\nFailure counter incremented on error.\nSuccess resets counter to 0.

state Open #4a3728/f5e6d3 : Tool blocked immediately.\nReturns CircuitOpen error.\nCooldown timer running (30s).

state HalfOpen #2a3a4a/cce5ff : Single test call allowed.\nNext result decides transition.

Closed --> Open : consecutive_failures\n>= threshold (3)
Open --> HalfOpen : cooldown elapsed (30s)
HalfOpen --> Closed : test call succeeds
HalfOpen --> Open : test call fails\n(reset cooldown)

note right of Closed
  Each tool has an independent
  circuit breaker instance.
  Failures are tracked per tool_id.
end note

note left of Open
  EventBus emission:
  CLOSED -> OPEN : CircuitBroken { tool_id, failures }
  * -> CLOSED : CircuitRestored { tool_id }
end note

note bottom of HalfOpen
  Only ONE concurrent call
  is permitted in HALF_OPEN.
  Additional calls return
  CircuitOpen until resolved.
end note

@enduml
